  "displayTimeZone": "Australia/Sydney",
  "header": "A voice you cannot download yet, a harness that mostly buys tokens, and a binder that is not a drug",
  "friendlyHeader": "A new voice model is not for download yet. A binder is not a medicine.",
  "summary": "Today's issue is about what you can actually use, and what the claim leaves out. Block has shown Dessa, a speech-only conversation model that runs on a high-end laptop, and is not offering it to the public yet. A study finds that swapping coding-agent harnesses moves scores about as much as running the same setup twice, while the bill can triple. The Verge reports that a widely shared drug-design experiment produced binders, not a scorpion antivenom. A patent-lawyer trial, a market chart, and a database check all point the same way: the useful question is what is still true after the model says it is done.",
  "friendlySummary": "Today is about what you can actually use, and what the claim leaves out. Block has shown Dessa, a conversation model trained only on speech. It can run on a high-end laptop. The public cannot download it yet. A study finds that changing the wrapper around a coding agent barely moves the score, but it can triple the bill. The Verge reports that a widely shared drug experiment made proteins that stick to a toxin. That is not an antivenom. A lawyer trial, a market chart, and a database check all say the same thing. Ask what is still true after the model says it is finished.",
